{"Two non-development requests that both see an empty cache can queue on the write lock, but the second request never checks whether the first one already populated entryPointAssetsCache, causing it to re-read the manifest and potentially replace a valid cache with nil if that second read hits a transient file error": 0.9800111055374146, "When cfg.Env == setting.Dev, every request skips the cache fast path and holds a global write lock while opening and decoding assets-manifest.json, causing concurrent page loads and /api/frontend/settings/ calls to wait on each other for filesystem work that previously ran in parallel, making development servers noticeably slower on Docker or network filesystems": 0.8179656863212585}